## Ablation studies

CAMELYON16 ablations examine spatial connectivity, aggregation-head design, graph encoder depth/type, and sampling level. All configurations reuse the main model's training/validation slide identities and validation bag-level cross-entropy checkpoint-selection rule.

| Configuration | Change from the main model |
|---|---|
| A0: SC-CIA | One-layer, three-head GAT with eight-neighbor connectivity, the SC-CIA aggregation head, and joint bag/maximum-instance CE |
| A1 | Self-loop-only connectivity |
| A2 | DSMIL aggregation head |
| A3 | Alternative attention head without class-specific reference selection |
| B1 / B2 | Two-layer / three-layer GAT |
| B3 / B4 / B5 | One-layer / two-layer / three-layer GCN |
| C1 / C2 | Sampling Level 2 / Level 3 |

A0 is the same checkpoint reported under `results/CAMELYON16/main/SC-CIA/`; it is not a separate training run. The remaining ten configurations are stored under `results/CAMELYON16/ablation/`, with metrics, slide-level predictions, logs, and available configuration/split records.

A2 and A3 compare complete aggregation-head implementations. In particular, A3 changes reference selection, attention computation, and readout together; its performance difference must not be interpreted as the isolated effect of reference selection.

Results are from the corrected-label retest on 2026-11-20, using saved checkpoints rather than retraining. The retained test cohort contains 80 negative and 49 positive slides, with `test_114` labeled positive. Reported results are single-run observations, not multi-seed averages.
